1 over x minus 1.

00:32.846 --> 00:34.220
And you might say,
hey, Sal look,

00:34.220 --> 00:36.511
I have the same thing in the
numerator and denominator.

00:36.511 --> 00:38.480
If I have something
divided by itself,

00:38.480 --> 00:39.730
that would just be equal to 1.

00:39.730 --> 00:42.200
Can't I just simplify
this to f of x equals 1?

00:42.200 --> 00:44.750
And I would say, well,
you're almost true,

00:44.750 --> 00:46.860
the difference between
f of x equals 1

00:46.860 --> 00:50.300
and this thing right over here,
is that this thing can never

00:50.300 --> 00:54.200
equal-- this thing is
undefined when x is equal to 1.

00:54.200 --> 00:56.560
Because if you set,
let me define it.

00:56.560 --> 00:59.040
Let me write it over
here, if you have f of,

00:59.040 --> 01:02.650
sorry not f of 0, if you
have f of 1, what happens.

01:02.650 --> 01:04.599
In the numerator,
we get 1 minus 1,

01:04.599 --> 01:07.770
which is, let me just write
it down, in the numerator,

01:07.770 --> 01:08.910
you get 0.

01:08.910 --> 01:13.590
And in the denominator, you
get 1 minus 1, which is also 0.

01:13.590 --> 01:16.800
And so anything divided by
0, including 0 divided by 0,

01:16.800 --> 01:17.550
this is undefined.

01:21.350 --> 01:23.520
So you can make
the simplification.

01:23.520 --> 01:28.980
You can say that this is you the
same thing as f of x is equal

01:28.980 --> 01:35.080
to 1, but you would have to add
the constraint that x cannot be

01:35.080 --> 01:36.340
equal to 1.

01:36.340 --> 01:38.190
Now this and this
are equivalent,

01:38.190 --> 01:40.470
both of these are
going to be equal to 1

01:40.470 --> 01:44.820
for all other X's other
than one, but at x equals 1,

01:44.820 --> 01:46.070
it becomes undefined.

01:46.070 --> 01:48.770
This is undefined and
this one's undefined.

01:48.770 --> 01:51.540
So how would I
graph this function.

01:51.540 --> 01:54.610
So let me graph it.

01:54.610 --> 01:59.130
So that, is my y is
equal to f of x axis,

01:59.130 --> 02:04.330
y is equal to f of x axis,
and then this over here

02:04.330 --> 02:05.666
is my x-axis.

02:09.680 --> 02:12.940
And then let's say this is
